    "text": "Man Decided To Pull A Gun On An Off-Duty Cop During A Road Rage Incident...That Was His Last Mistake\nAn off-duty Milwaukee police officer shot and killed a man armed with a gun after a minor traffic crash, Milwaukee Police Chief Jeffrey Norman said.\nThe shooting happened on West Mill Road, near North 47th Street, at about 8:30 a.m. Oct. 9.\nNorman said after the crash, both men exited their vehicles. The driver drew a gun, hit the off-duty officer in the face with it, then the driver and officer exchanged gunfire, the chief said.",
